# skeletons.id is the SHA-256 of these files' exact bytes (content-addressed,
# see manage_skeleton.py); capture_persons.default_skeleton_id rows
# elsewhere reference that id directly. Without this, a checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (common on Windows) silently rewrites LF to CRLF,
# changing the hash and turning "Default male"/"Default female" into a
# *different* skeleton (identical content, new id) purely from checking the
# repo out -- confirmed reproducing exactly this way on 2026-08-23. -text
# disables line-ending conversion in both directions.
python/posetrak/data/skeletons/default_female.yaml -text
python/posetrak/data/skeletons/default_male.yaml -text
